      ],
      "independent_reason": "The current degree lemma supplies finite local freeness only for a nonzero integer, but the etaleness lemma allows d=0. A nonzero abelian variety has positive dimension: a zero-dimensional integral variety with a k-valued unit would be Spec(k). For d=0 the fibre over the unit is all of A, so local quasi-finiteness and hence etaleness fail. The added case split is valid without invoking the degree lemma in the zero case. For d nonzero the existing finite-flat and tangent argument applies, including when d is divisible by the field characteristic.",
      "nearby_registered_unit": "MC-STK-ERR-1494 repairs the hypothesis of the separate degree lemma at pinned line 1771. This new operation at pinned 1836 repairs its application in the etaleness proof and preserves the admitted degree-lemma repair.",
      "alternatives": "Do not add d!=0 to the etaleness statement: its current statement correctly includes and answers the zero case.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "confidence_reason": "The zero-case fibre gives a direct noncircular argument and the remaining degree-lemma hypothesis then matches."
    },
    {
      "local_name": "colimit-cover-orientation",
      "verdict": "VALID_NOT_DUPLICATE",
      "source_label": "lemma-colimit-kappa",
      "current_contexts": [
