      ],
      "independent_reason": "The map alpha has source t*F and target s*F. Therefore alpha on W_ijk has source M_i tensor_(A_i,t) B_ijk and target M_j tensor_(A_j,s) B_ijk, which requires t(W_ijk) inside U_i and s(W_ijk) inside U_j. Swapping s and t in the cover provides exactly these structure maps while preserving every later index. The finite-support closure yields alpha(t*G) contained in s*G. Pullback by inversion, followed by alpha and the inverse identity, yields the reverse containment. Thus the later equality remains justified.",
      "nearby_registered_units": [
        "MC-STK-ERR-1504 removes duplicated wording in the cardinal comparison at pinned 3183.",
        "MC-STK-ERR-1505 corrects the identity support-choice indices at pinned 3215-3216."
      ],
      "alternatives": "Reversing alpha globally or swapping all downstream i,j indices would alter the fixed convention. No compatibility of particular inverse cover members is needed for the global inclusion/inversion argument.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "confidence_reason": "The two required tensor-product structure maps determine the cover orientation uniquely."
    },
    {
      "local_name": "invariants-base-change-coefficient-ring",
      "verdict": "VALID_NOT_DUPLICATE",
      "source_label": "lemma-invariants-base-change",
      "current_contexts": [
