        ]
      ],
      "independent_reason": "The componentwise assertion is part (2)(a) for A_r,B_r,C_r,C'_r,C^1_r, so its polynomial belongs to C'_r[x]. The constant-rank norm proof explicitly maps D[x] into C'[x]. Invariant rank strata yield a finite product decomposition; raising each component polynomial to n/r and gluing over C' preserves the claim. Independently, the identity groupoid over a field k, base changed to k[z], has rank one and f=z. The needed polynomial is x-z, which lies in k[z][x] and cannot come from k[x].",
      "nearby_registered_unit": "MC-STK-ERR-1515 changes Spec(C') to Spec(A') at pinned 4421/current 4715. The polynomial-ring correction at pinned 4425/current 4719 is distinct and leaves that admitted correction intact.",
      "alternatives": "Changing the final gluing ring to C would fail the identity-groupoid counterexample.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "confidence_reason": "The norm's codomain, component gluing, and rank-one counterexample independently force the prime."
    },
    {
      "local_name": "colimit-two-ambient-modules",
